{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Testing Blender API Calls.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Testing Blender API Calls.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"testing blender api calls testing blender api calls","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Testing Blender API Calls.md","fileName":"Testing Blender API Calls.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Testing Blender API Calls","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Scripting Environment]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Scripting Environment","Blender Interactive Console","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Testing Blender API Calls.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Testing Blender API Calls.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"testing blender api calls testing blender api calls","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Testing Blender API Calls.md","fileName":"Testing Blender API Calls.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Testing Blender API Calls","heading":"Testing Blender API Calls","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A Blender API call is easiest to understand when it is reduced and tested interactively before being placed in a longer script. Optional arguments copied from the interface can be removed one at a time, while the viewport and data inspectors reveal which changes the remaining call actually performs.\n\nTesting must account for Blender state. Mode, selected objects, the active object, and the current area can change the meaning or availability of an operator. Small trials in the [[Blender Interactive Console]] isolate those dependencies before they become hidden inside a larger automation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Scripting Environment","Blender Interactive Console","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"propert